Z||000000||Beaverman||12-23-2001||03:09 PM||||Hrm got a question to ask all you knowledable people. <P>I've changed out the heater motor/and the switch inside the car and i still can't get the fan to work.  No airflow at all when i switch between the lo hi's.  I own a 87 gt, and i took the parts off my old part car thats an 86 gt.  And yet i still get no airflow.  Any ideas what the problem is?<P>Thanks||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||12-23-2001||03:12 PM||||exactly what speeds are affected? List them all from low to high.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000002||Beaverman||12-23-2001||03:17 PM||||No speed works.  I get no airflow at all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-23-2001||03:42 PM||||In a non AC car there's not much to that... only other thing I see in the wire diegrams that would kill all speeds is the fuse or the motor not grounded.<P>In an AC car the fuse, AC controls, or the AC relay could do it. <P>AC cars use 2 realys. one is for the blower's high speed, the other is the AC power according to the wire diagram. I don't remember where that relays are. I think in the spare tire bay. <P>I think the two relays are the same so to test you could simply trade the plugs. At that point the heater should work on the first 3 speeds but not high.<P>If one of them turns out bad just replace both. they aren't very expensive.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||12-23-2001||03:46 PM||||The fan doesn't run? Or no airflow? If the latter, my old Jeep had the wires attached the wrong way causing the fan to run backwards.  Because of the fan design this meant lots of fan noise but no air flow.<BR>Gary||||reg||5
Z||000005||rogergarrison||12-23-2001||06:54 PM||||theres a set of reostats/resistors in the front compartment in the middle on the firewall (backside of dash) about even with the spring that pops the front hood up. Its right next to the silver tank looking thing if you have AC and near the back of the jack. Its a flat plastic plug with i think 4 wires. take out the 2 8mm screws and pull them out to see if any are burned in 2. Real cheap to replace. That will cause no power to get to fan even if fuse is good.||||reg||1
